        "original_id": "dbb26039-962f-55bc-a9f9-cdd3b699a622",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ron de Moraes\n- Roles: television director, producer\n- Events: 2002 Winter Olympics opening ceremony, Disney Parks Christmas Day Parade\n- Organizations: ABC\n- Places: Magic Kingdom, Walt Disney World Resort, Orlando, Florida\n- Topics: American television specials, awards\n\nFacts:\n- Ron de Moraes is an American television director and producer.\n- Ron de Moraes has worked on numerous commercials, shows, and concerts.\n- Ron de Moraes received an Emmy Award for co-directing the 2002 Winter Olympics opening ceremony.\n- Ron de Moraes received a Daytime Emmy Award for his work on the 2007 Disney Parks Christmas Day Parade.\n- The Disney Parks Christmas Day Parade is an American television special that airs on Christmas Day on ABC.\n- The Disney Parks Christmas Day Parade is taped primarily inside the Magic Kingdom at Walt Disney World Resort in Orlando, Florida, about one month before Christmas Day.",
